\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Per-example overlap appears stable from minimal attention across benchmarks. (a,\,b) LAMBADA: cross-architecture $\sigma $ shows a non-significant decreasing trend at 1.3B (solid; Bonferroni-adjusted $p = .167$) but partially rebounds at 340M (dashed), while pairwise Jaccard of helped/hurt sets appears stable from 4\% attention onward. (c) This pattern holds across all four main benchmarks: mean pairwise $\bar  {J}$ remains flat across attention ratios (all $\rho \leq 0.80$, $p \geq .333$). Shaded bands are illustrative ($n = 3$).}}{2}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:decoupling}{{1}{2}{Per-example overlap appears stable from minimal attention across benchmarks. (a,\,b) LAMBADA: cross-architecture $\sigma $ shows a non-significant decreasing trend at 1.3B (solid; Bonferroni-adjusted $p = .167$) but partially rebounds at 340M (dashed), while pairwise Jaccard of helped/hurt sets appears stable from 4\% attention onward. (c) This pattern holds across all four main benchmarks: mean pairwise $\bar {J}$ remains flat across attention ratios (all $\rho \leq 0.80$, $p \geq .333$). Shaded bands are illustrative ($n = 3$)}{figure.caption.1}{}}
